{title: 332 - The Cleansing Wave}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #332 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: D}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 332}
{meta: category Gospel - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D/F#]Oh now I see the crimson [G]wave, The fountain deep [F#m]and wide;
[F#m]Jesus, my Lord, [A]mighty [D/F#]to save, Points to His wounded [F#m]side.
[G]The cleansing stream I see, I see, [F#m]I plunge, and O, it [Em/G]cleanseth [D/F#]me!
[F#m]O praise [G]the Lord! it cleanseth [Bm]me, [D/A]It cleanseth me, yes, cleanseth [A]me.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[A7]The cleansing [C#7]stream [D]I see, I see,
[F#m]I plunge, [G]and O, it cleanseth [Bm]me!
[D/A]O praise the Lord! it cleanseth [A]me,
[A7]It cleanseth me, yes, cleanseth [D/F#]me.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D/F#]I see the new [G]creation [F#m]rise,
[F#m]I hear [A]the [D/A]speaking blood;
[G]It speaks polluted [F#m]nature [Em/G]dies,
[F#m]Sinks [G]'neath the [D/A]cleansing [A]flood.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[D/F#]I rise to walk in [G]heaven's own [F#m]light,
[F#m]Above [A]the [D/A]world and sin;
[G]With heart made pure [F#m]and garments [Em/G]white,
[F#m]And [G]Christ enthroned [D]within.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[D/F#]Amazing grace! 'tis [G]heaven below
[F#m]To feel [D/F#]the blood applied,
[G]And Jesus, only [F#m]Jesus, [Em/G]know,
[F#m]My [G]Jesus [D/A]crucified.
{end_of_verse}
